msgid "Asynchronous generators best practices"
msgstr "非同期ジェネレーターを使う際の推奨事項"

msgid ""
"Writing correct and efficient asyncio code requires awareness of certain "
"pitfalls. This section outlines essential best practices that can save you "
"hours of debugging."
msgstr ""
"正しく効率的な asyncio コードを書くには、いくつかの落とし穴を知っておく必要が"
"あります。\n"
"この節では、長時間のデバッグを避けるために役立つ重要な実践方法を説明します。"

msgid "Close asynchronous generators explicitly"
msgstr "非同期ジェネレーターを明示的に閉じる"

msgid ""
"It is recommended to manually close the :term:`asynchronous generator "
"<asynchronous generator iterator>`. If a generator exits early - for "
"example, due to an exception raised in the body of an ``async for`` loop - "
"its asynchronous cleanup code may run in an unexpected context. This can "
"occur after the tasks it depends on have completed, or during the event loop "
"shutdown when the async-generator's garbage collection hook is called."
msgstr ""
":term:`非同期ジェネレーター <asynchronous generator iterator>` は明示的に閉じ"
"ることを推奨します。\n"
"例えば ``async for`` ループの本体で例外が起きるなどして、途中でジェネレーター"
"の使用を終えると、非同期の後始末処理が予期しないコンテキストで実行される可能"
"性があります。\n"
"依存するタスクが完了した後や、イベントループの終了中に非同期ジェネレーターの"
"ガベージコレクション用フックが呼び出されたときに、後始末が行われることがあり"
"ます。"

msgid ""
"To avoid this, explicitly close the generator by calling its :meth:`~agen."
"aclose` method, or use the :func:`contextlib.aclosing` context manager::"
msgstr ""
"これを避けるには、:meth:`~agen.aclose` メソッドを呼び出して明示的にジェネレー"
"ターを閉じるか、:func:`contextlib.aclosing` コンテキストマネージャーを使って"
"ください。 ::"

msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import contextlib\n"
"\n"
"async def gen():\n"
"  yield 1\n"
"  yield 2\n"
"\n"
"async def func():\n"
"  async with contextlib.aclosing(gen()) as g:\n"
"    async for x in g:\n"
"      break  # Don't iterate until the end\n"
"\n"
"asyncio.run(func())"
msgstr ""
"import asyncio\n"
"import contextlib\n"
"\n"
"async def gen():\n"
"  yield 1\n"
"  yield 2\n"
"\n"
"async def func():\n"
"  async with contextlib.aclosing(gen()) as g:\n"
"    async for x in g:\n"
"      break  # 最後までイテレーションしない\n"
"\n"
"asyncio.run(func())"

msgid ""
"As noted above, the cleanup code for these asynchronous generators is "
"deferred. The following example demonstrates that the finalization of an "
"asynchronous generator can occur in an unexpected order::"
msgstr ""
"前述のとおり、これらの非同期ジェネレーターの後始末処理は後回しにされます。\n"
"次の例は、非同期ジェネレーターの終了処理が予期しない順序で行われる場合を示し"
"ています。 ::"

msgid ""
"import asyncio\n"
"work_done = False\n"
"\n"
"async def cursor():\n"
"    try:\n"
"        yield 1\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        assert work_done\n"
"\n"
"async def rows():\n"
"    global work_done\n"
"    try:\n"
"        yield 2\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        await asyncio.sleep(0.1) # imitate some async work\n"
"        work_done = True\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"async def main():\n"
"    async for c in cursor():\n"
"        async for r in rows():\n"
"            break\n"
"        break\n"
"\n"
"asyncio.run(main())"
msgstr ""
"import asyncio\n"
"work_done = False\n"
"\n"
"async def cursor():\n"
"    try:\n"
"        yield 1\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        assert work_done\n"
"\n"
"async def rows():\n"
"    global work_done\n"
"    try:\n"
"        yield 2\n"
"    finally:\n"
"        await asyncio.sleep(0.1) # 非同期の処理を模倣する\n"
"        work_done = True\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"async def main():\n"
"    async for c in cursor():\n"
"        async for r in rows():\n"
"            break\n"
"        break\n"
"\n"
"asyncio.run(main())"

msgid "For this example, we get the following output::"
msgstr "この例の出力は次のようになります。 ::"

